  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-free-web-search",
      "text": "Free web search plugin for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness). No API keys required — works out of the box with Bing, DuckDuckGo, and SearXNG. Optional paid engines (Exa, Tavily, Keenable, Perplexity, DeepSeek Official) activate when you add a key."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **10 search engines** with automatic fallback — if one fails, the next one picks up\n- **Time-filtered search** via `advanced_search` tool (last day/week/month/year, or custom ranges like `3d`, `2mo`, `2026-07-01`)\n- **Platform search** — GitHub repos and Reddit threads via `platform_search` tool\n- **Engine diagnostics** — `free_search_test` tool to check which engines work\n- **Web Settings UI** — engine selection, API key management, cache TTL config\n- **Result caching** — LRU cache (50 entries, configurable TTL up to 5 min) to reduce rate limiting"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:delef/dsh-free-web-search\n```\n\nIf pnpm blocks the build script, add the key it prints to `allowBuilds` in your profile's `pnpm-workspace.yaml` and retry."
    },
    {
      "section": "Engines",
      "text": "| Engine | Cost | Key required |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| Bing | Free | No |\n| DuckDuckGo (HTML / Lite) | Free | No |\n| SearXNG | Free | No |\n| AnySearch AI | Free | No |\n| Exa | Free tier / paid | Optional |\n| Tavily | Free tier / paid | Optional |\n| Keenable | Free tier / paid | Optional |\n| Perplexity | Paid | Yes |\n| DeepSeek Official | Paid | Yes |\n\nDefault engine: **Bing** (most stable). Change it in Settings > Plugins > Free Web Search, or type `/free-search-engine` in chat."
    },
    {
      "section": "`web_search` (built-in, powered by this plugin)",
      "text": "Standard harness web search. Uses the configured engine with automatic fallback."
    },
    {
      "section": "`advanced_search`",
      "text": "```\nquery: \"rust async runtime\"\ntimeRange: \"week\"        # day | week | month | year | 3d | 2mo | 1y | 2026-07-01\nengine: \"exa\"            # optional, override preferred engine\nmaxResults: 5"
    },
    {
      "section": "`platform_search`",
      "text": "```\nplatform: \"github\"       # github | reddit\nquery: \"deepseek harness plugins\"\nmaxResults: 5\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "`web_fetch`",
      "text": "```\nurl: \"https://docs.example.com/guide\"\nmaxLength: 50000                       # optional, default 50000 chars\n```\n\nFetches a single page, strips HTML, returns plain text. For reading articles, docs, or any URL."
    },
    {
      "section": "`free_search_test`",
      "text": "Tests engine availability. No arguments tests all engines."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "Settings are managed through the web UI (Settings > Plugins > Free Web Search) or in the `free-web-search` entry of the active profile (DSH 0.2+; earlier releases used the `free-search` section of `settings.yaml`):\n\n```yaml\n- id: free-web-search\n  name: dsh-free-web-search\n  config:\n    provider: bing"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "Profiles that still use the old entry id `web-search-free` keep working, but the plugin logs a deprecation warning and the settings card shows a notice. Rename the entry to `free-web-search` to migrate.\n\nRequires DSH `>=0.2.0-rc.2` (developed against `0.2.1-rc.5`)."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "Apache-2.0"
    }
  ],
